# 10. Multiclass Logistic Regression

What happens when there are more than two classes?

Example:

```text
Animal Image:

Cat
Dog
Bird
Horse
```

There are two common approaches.

---

## A. One-vs-Rest (OvR)

Create multiple binary classifiers.

Example:

```text
Cat vs Everything
Dog vs Everything
Bird vs Everything
```

Choose the class with the strongest prediction.

---

## B. Softmax / Multinomial Logistic Regression

Softmax generalizes probabilities across multiple classes.

\[
\boxed{
P(y=k)=
\frac{e^{z_k}}
{\sum_j e^{z_j}}
}
\]

Example:

```text
Cat   → 0.10
Dog   → 0.70
Bird  → 0.15
Horse → 0.05
```

Prediction:

```text
DOG 🐶
```

Because it has the highest probability.

