# 11. Edge Cases and Failure Modes 🚨

## ❌ Highly Nonlinear Data

Logistic Regression creates a linear decision boundary in the original feature space.

For complex nonlinear patterns, consider:

- Polynomial features
- Decision Trees
- Random Forest
- Gradient Boosting
- Neural Networks
- Kernel methods such as SVM

---

## ❌ Imbalanced Data

Suppose:

```text
99% Genuine
1% Fraud
```

A model predicting:

```text
Always Genuine
```

could achieve:

```text
99% Accuracy
```

But it would be useless for fraud detection.

Therefore, don't rely only on accuracy.

Use:

- Precision
- Recall
- F1-score
- PR-AUC
- ROC-AUC

---

## ❌ Multicollinearity

Highly correlated features can make coefficient interpretation unstable.

---

## ❌ Data Leakage

Example:

Predicting whether a loan defaults using a feature created after the default decision.

This produces unrealistic performance.

